WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.924
Step three prints the nine decisions:

2
00:00:02.924 --> 00:00:06.725
each contractor's action,
earliest end and reason.

3
00:00:06.725 --> 00:00:08.650
Look at the four inactive ones.

4
00:00:08.650 --> 00:00:13.687
Each is inactive for a different reason:
a completion date, suitability withdrawn,

5
00:00:13.687 --> 00:00:18.650
a sponsor gone past the grace period, and
a sponsor recertification that came due.

6
00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:21.233
The last one is the knowledge-check case:

7
00:00:21.233 --> 00:00:24.913
whatever the contract says,
the earliest condition wins.

8
00:00:24.913 --> 00:00:29.671
The two quarantined records are nine
hundred thousand and seven, which has no

9
00:00:29.671 --> 00:00:32.720
contract end, and nine
hundred thousand and eight,

10
00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:34.876
whose sponsor isn't in the HR export.

11
00:00:34.876 --> 00:00:37.750
Step four hands the
extract to the middleware.

12
00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:40.654
It reports seven records
ready, in one batch,

13
00:00:40.654 --> 00:00:44.688
and four of them are disables,
the four inactive contractors.

14
00:00:44.688 --> 00:00:49.680
Nothing is held, and nothing is sent:
the middleware only builds the requests.
